        try: put the cursor on Colour and press Ctrl+Alt+T twice
        expected: Colour becomes the header Colour then hue then shade divided by pipes, and back to its three lines
    - B08 Blank Lines Become Dividers
        area: flip
        fixture: Phase below
        try: put the cursor on Phase and press Ctrl+Alt+T twice
        expected: the table carries a divider under the header and one between Design and Build; flipped back, the blank lines are where they were
    - B09 A Concept Default
        area: defaults
        fixture: Currency and Outlay below
        try: hover the name Rent; hover EUR on the currency line of Lunch and Ctrl+click it; then under Rent type currency and a colon and press Ctrl+Space
        expected: the hover of Rent lists currency EUR as the default of Currency; EUR under Lunch is underlined dotted and lands on the Currency line; the completion offers EUR
    - B10 Defaults In A Header
        area: defaults
        fixture: Plan below
        try: hover the name Starter; then save this file and open aot.files/Plan.csv
        expected: the hover of Starter lists seats 1 from Plan; the CSV has Starter with 10 and 1 and Team with 40 and 5, and no row for Basic, which is the default and not an Example
    - B11 Equals Defines And A Doubled Equals Is Literal
        area: syntax
        fixture: Quote below
        try: hover the name Q1, and look at the colours on the vat line of Quote and on the note line of Q1
        expected: the hover lists the note with one equals sign between a and b; the Python after the single equals sign of vat is coloured as code, and the doubled equals of the note as an escape
    - B12 The CSV Mirror Writes Back
        area: csv
        fixture: Stock below, and aot.files/Stock.csv after a save
        try: save this file; hover the name Stock and click Open Stock.csv; in the CSV change Bolt to 6 and save it, then back to 5 and save it; then empty the count of Washer in the CSV and save it
        expected: the link opens the CSV; after each CSV save this file changes and saves itself; Bolt reads 6, then 5 again, and the count cell of Washer is empty
    - B13 A CSV Saved Last Overrides Unsaved Edits And Drops Rows
        area: csv
        fixture: Stock below and aot.files/Stock.csv
        try: change Washer here and do not save; delete the Screw row from the CSV and save it
        expected: Washer goes back to what the CSV says and Screw goes from this file, with nothing asked; this file stays unsaved until you save it
    - B14 The File Saved Last Overrides The Other
        area: csv
        fixture: Stock below, aot.files/Stock.csv, and the setting aot.tableCsvSyncMode
        try: set the setting to manual; change Nut to 4 and Bolt to 7 here and save; change Nut to 8 in the CSV and save it; press Ctrl+K Y; then change Bolt to 9 in the CSV and save it, change Nut to 3 here and save, and press Ctrl+K Y; afterwards set the setting back to auto
        expected: nothing syncs until Ctrl+K Y; the first time the CSV was saved last, so here Nut reads 8 and Bolt goes back to what the CSV says; the second time this file was saved last, so the CSV has Nut 3 and Bolt goes back to what this file says; no notice either time
